PROBES=('import', 'one_symbol', 'schemata_pi', 'input_redundancy', 'input_redundancy_sample', 'edge_redundancy', 'edge_redundancy_sample', 'bias', 'sensitivity_bit_lut', 'sensitivity_schemata', 'input_symmetry')

=== probe methods ===
  import                    detached positional import → BooleanNode (no LUT / no covers)
  one_symbol                expression cascade → one-symbol primes/schemata (no LUT / no covers)
  schemata_pi               PI schemata DataFrame from derived primes (no full covers)
  input_redundancy          exact k_r: force full pi_coverage (exact_k_max=k); refuses / times out when Θ(2**k) cover is too large
  input_redundancy_sample   sample covers: estimate k_r from n=16384 minterms (match covering PIs; no pi_coverage dict)
  edge_redundancy           exact r_i: force full pi_coverage (exact_k_max=k); refuses / times out when Θ(2**k) cover is too large
  edge_redundancy_sample    sample covers: estimate r_i from n=16384 minterms (match covering PIs; no pi_coverage dict)
  bias                      build dense LUT (get_bit_lut), then popcount / 2**k
  sensitivity_bit_lut       exact s: build dense LUT (get_bit_lut), then single-flip average sensitivity; refuses above MAX_DENSE_LUT_K
  sensitivity_schemata      sample covers: estimate s from n=16384 minterms via sensitivity_from_schemata (upper edge effectiveness; exact_k_max=-1; no pi_coverage dict)
  input_symmetry            exact k_s: build full ts_coverage over all 2**k minterms

